// Data of the theorem graph (theorems.html): theorems, lemmas, corollaries and conjectures of algebraic number theory,
// MSC 2020 11R (global fields) and 11S (local fields). In English. Built on 3 November 2026: the 19 theorems with first
// class 11R or 11S and Minkowski's convex body theorem (11H, used only here, area "basic" until geometry of numbers has a
// folder) moved here from ../../arithmetic-geometry/data/theorem-graph.js with their ids (rule 1 of ../../CLAUDE.md),
// the rest added.
//
// Model as in ../../arithmetic-geometry/data/theorem-graph.js (see its header comment): `premises` and `proof` are the
// standard textbook proof, named in `proofName`; further proofs in `alternativeProofs`; `foundation: true` marks general
// tools. `area` is the five-character class for 11R and "11S" for local fields, as in data/concepts.js. `concepts` are
// ids of data/concepts.js or carry the prefix of another folder.
// References to theorems of other folders: "ent:", "gt:", "ca:" (Dedekind domains, Hensel's lemma, Chinese remainder
// theorem), "ar:" (Galois theory, Kummer theory, Poisson summation, L-functions, modular forms).
//
// Sources: Neukirch, Algebraic Number Theory (1999); Marcus, Number Fields (1977); Washington, Introduction to
// Cyclotomic Fields (2nd ed. 1997); Cassels and Fröhlich, Algebraic Number Theory (1967); Serre, Local Fields (1979);
// Milne, Class Field Theory (notes, 2020); Cox, Primes of the Form x² + ny² (1989). Not checked by a specialist.
// Checked by ../../tests/check-theorems.js.
// `fromDefinitions: true` marks a theorem whose usual proof uses only definitions and axioms of its area and no
// theorem (it has no premises); a theorem without premises that rests on theory outside these graphs carries
// `foundation: true`, and its `proof` names that theory. tests/check-theorems.js warns about theorems without
// premises that have neither mark.

